Date: Mon, 7 Sep 2026 17:54:42 +0300
Subject: [PATCH 65/71] Let glm-5.3-flash accept image input

The catalog entry added in `6a5e29fa1d` declared `input_modalities: ["text"]`,
so `view_image` refused every call with "view_image is not allowed because you
do not support image inputs" - three times across the recorded sessions - while
its spec still cost about 230 tokens of the fixed prefix on every request.

GLM 5.3 Flash is natively multimodal: images are a first-class input to the same
model in the same call, passed as `image_url` blocks with either a URL or a
base64 data URL, and billed as ordinary input tokens. The Chat request builder
already emits exactly that shape, so nothing but the declaration was missing.

Verified live: `view_image` on a 64x64 checkerboard, and the model described the
pattern. `supports_image_detail_original` stays false; the Chat wire drops the
detail field and Z.ai documents no equivalent.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 codex-rs/models-manager/models.json | 3 ++-
 1 file changed, 2 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/codex-rs/models-manager/models.json b/codex-rs/models-manager/models.json
index 0b8530d3de..f650abd332 100644
--- a/codex-rs/models-manager/models.json
+++ b/codex-rs/models-manager/models.json
@@ -8,7 +8,8 @@
       "apply_patch_tool_type": "freeform",
       "web_search_tool_type": "text_and_image",
       "input_modalities": [
-        "text"
+        "text",
+        "image"
       ],
       "supports_image_detail_original": false,
       "truncation_policy": {
